{"id":"mortar","name":"Mortar","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:mortar"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Mortar","text":"(Heb. homer), cement of lime and sand (Gen. 11:3; Ex. 1:14); also potter’s clay (Isa. 41:25; Nah. 3:14). Also Heb. ‘aphar, usually rendered “dust,” clay or mud used for cement in building (Lev. 14:42, 45). Mortar for pulverizing (Prov. 27:22) grain or other substances by means of a pestle instead of a mill. Mortars were used in the wilderness for pounding the manna (Num. 11:8). It is commonly used in Palestine at the present day to pound wheat, from which the Arabs make a favourite dish called kibby."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H2563","lemma":"חֹמֶר","xlit":"chômer","gloss":"a bubbling up","kjv":"clay, heap, homer, mire","count":4,"share":0.44},{"strong":"H3843","lemma":"לְבֵנָה","xlit":"lᵉbênâh","gloss":"a brick","kjv":"brick, tile","count":2,"share":0.22},{"strong":"H2902","lemma":"טוּחַ","xlit":"ṭûwach","gloss":"to smear, especially with lime","kjv":"daub, overlay, plaister, smut","count":2,"share":0.22},{"strong":"H2916","lemma":"טִיט","xlit":"ṭîyṭ","gloss":"mud or clay","kjv":"clay, dirt, mire","count":2,"share":0.22},{"strong":"H68","lemma":"אֶבֶן","xlit":"ʼeben","gloss":"a stone","kjv":"carbuncle, mason, plummet, stone","count":3,"share":0.33},{"strong":"H7429","lemma":"רָמַס","xlit":"râmaç","gloss":"to tread upon","kjv":"oppressor, stamp upon, trample, tread","count":2,"share":0.22}],"verses":["Gen.11.3","Exod.1.14","Isa.41.25","Nah.3.14","Lev.14.42","Lev.14.45","Num.11.8","Prov.27.22","Ezek.22.28"],"related":[{"id":"grinding","type":"seealso","why":"Nave's Topical Bible lists it under See also"},{"id":"mill","type":"seealso","why":"Nave's Topical Bible lists it under See also"},{"id":"brick","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.111,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"house","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.038,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"houses","type":"coocc